wn from a population with the population mean $\\mu .$ \nThen, the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}.\n$$\n\nNote that:\n\n- $\\overset{―}{X}$ is the mean value of ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{n},$ while $\\overset{¯}{x}$ is the mean of a specific sample ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n},$\n\n- the sample mean $\\overset{―}{X}$ is an estimator of the population mean $\\mu ,$ and\n\n- the value $\\overset{^}{\\mu }=\\overset{¯}{x}$ is an estimate of the population mean $\\mu .$\n\nTherefore, our estimate for the population mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{^}{\\mu } & =\\overset{―}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{8}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}(-9-4+1+7-3+6+10+12) \\\\  & =\\frac{20}{8} \\\\  & =2.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-89547a27-782d-5edb-a84a-c342d94aab57"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-89547a27-782d-5edb-a84a-c342d94aab57" :answer-field/id #uuid "89547a27-782d-5edb-a84a-c342d94aab57" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ef41a907-369a-5ca3-9f40-ac473c2bc7f2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ef41a907-369a-5ca3-9f40-ac473c2bc7f2" "answer-2c9c2705-b383-5552-8765-afa77e795806" "answer-0a29066f-c5c6-5f13-9704-332d81aafa1e" "answer-9d1a5509-8a63-5798-9db0-2a0cde6f6ed1" "answer-1e63e961-b7cd-57a7-b177-22138ad08e0f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ef41a907-369a-5ca3-9f40-ac473c2bc7f2" :answer/id #uuid "ef41a907-369a-5ca3-9f40-ac473c2bc7f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c9c2705-b383-5552-8765-afa77e795806" :answer/id #uuid "2c9c2705-b383-5552-8765-afa77e795806" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3.0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a29066f-c5c6-5f13-9704-332d81aafa1e" :answer/id #uuid "0a29066f-c5c6-5f13-9704-332